{
  "outcome": "needs_user_info",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Sofia, sorry about the Teams trouble. Please try these steps. First, in Teams go to Settings, then Devices, and make sure the correct microphone, speaker and camera are selected, especially if you use a headset or docking station. Next, check that the physical mute key is off and that any camera privacy shutter is open. Close other apps that might be using the camera, such as Zoom or browser tabs with video calls. Then fully quit Teams (right-click its taskbar icon and choose Quit) and reopen it. You can also use Teams' 'Make a test call' option to check your audio. If the camera and microphone still don't work after a restart, please reply and tell us whether Windows shows the camera at all and whether the problem happens on every call. That will help us decide on next steps.",
  "internal_note": "User Sofia Rossi (ID 7, Marketing) is active, not locked, no failed logins, and her recent sign-ins are normal: VPN from residential IP and M365 from corporate IP, all Duo push, within usual hours. Assigned laptop BL-LT-0107 shows offline with no check-in for 12 days (last 2026-09-29), though the user has been signing in daily since. Disk is fine (54.7% free). The laptop status may be stale, or the user may be working from another device, so verify which device she uses. I could not check whether Windows detects the camera. Walked the user through KB-025 quick checks and fix steps. Escalate to Tier 2 / hardware if the camera is not detected by Windows or the problem persists after restart. No account actions were taken.",
